      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-139407",
      ":question/problem": "The $100$ employees of a small company are classified according to their age and weekly salary. The HR manager notes the following:\n\n- All employees are paid $$400$, $$600$, or $$800$ per week.\n- $65$ employees are aged under $35$.\n- $2$ of the $10$ employees who are paid $$800$ are aged under $35$.\n- $17$ of the $35$ employees who are paid $$600$ are aged $35$ or older.\n\nUse a joint frequency table to determine how many employees who are paid $$400$ are aged under $35$."
    },
