      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-139408",
      ":question/problem": "In a college, $200$ students were asked about their preferred sport. The interviewer notes the following:\n\n- All students prefer baseball, football, or tennis.\n- $60$ students prefer baseball.\n- Of the students who prefer football, $15$ are female.\n- $35$ of the $120$ male students prefer baseball and $30$ prefer tennis.\n\nUse a joint frequency table to determine how many female students prefer tennis."
